{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` priors for `sigma_a1`, `sigma_a2`, and `sigma_y`. These parameters already had finite bounds `real<lower=0, upper=100>`, so the added built-in uniform sampling statements are density-neutral for the original constrained-parameter model and satisfy SafeStan's unique-prior requirement. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> person;
  vector[N] time;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] eta1;
  vector[J] eta2;
  real mu_a1;
  real mu_a2;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a1;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a2;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] a1;
  vector[J] a2;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  a1 = mu_a1 + sigma_a1 * eta1;
  a2 = 0.1 * mu_a2 + sigma_a2 * eta2;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a1[person[i]] + a2[person[i]] * time[i];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_a2 ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta2 ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a1 ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_a2 ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":4,"person":[1,1,1,1],"time":[1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0],"y":[2.0,4.0,4.0,4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
